/*
 * Declares the ModuleRefValue class.
 *
 * ModuleRefValue represents a reference to a module in the generator IR. It is
 * a special kind of named value: unlike VarRefValue or GlobalVarRefValue, it
 * does not refer to a variable, but to a module symbol itself.
 *
 * Module references appear when resolving qualified names (e.g. `foo::bar`)
 * where `foo` is a module. They behave like immutable, non-lvalue values whose
 * type is `None`, since modules are not runtime values.
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::variable::module
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/variable/module.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-02-27
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
